ConceptKey Pointsuper()Returns a proxy delegating to the next class in MROZero-arg super()Python 3 only — shorthand for super(__class__, self)MROsuper() follows MRO, not the literal parentHardcoded parentAnimal.__init__(self) — breaks in multiple inheritance__init__ ruleCall super().__init__() first, before any child attribute setupCooperative MIEvery class calls super() — each grandparent runs exactly once@classmethodsuper() works — cls is used instead of self@staticmethodsuper() zero-arg form fails — use explicit super(B, cls) or restructure

Exercises
E1. Build a three-level chain Person → Employee → Manager. Each adds one attribute in __init__. Use super() at every level. Print all attributes on a Manager instance and verify none are missing.
E2. Create a diamond:
    A
   / \
  B   C
   \ /
    D

Give each class an __init__ that calls super().__init__() and prints its class name. Instantiate D and verify A.__init__ prints exactly once. Then replace super() with hardcoded parent calls and observe it prints twice.
E3. Write a ValidationMixin with a method validate(self, data) that checks data is not None. Write a LoggingMixin with validate(self, data) that prints &quot;Validating...&quot; then calls super().validate(data). Write a Processor class inheriting from LoggingMixin, ValidationMixin with validate that calls super().validate(data) then processes. Trace the MRO and verify the call order.
E4. Override __init__ in a TimedList(list) subclass that adds a self.created_at timestamp. Use super().__init__(*args, **kwargs) to pass all arguments to list.__init__. Verify the result behaves like a normal list plus has the timestamp attribute.
E5 (Design). Implement a mini nn.Module-style system: Module base with parameters() returning [], forward(x) raising NotImplementedError. Linear(Module) adds a weight list and implements forward. ReLU(Module) implements forward(x) as max(0, x) elementwise. Sequential(Module) stores a list of modules, overrides parameters() to return combined parameters from all children via super(), and chains forward through all modules.

